+
+# Technical Design
+
+## Context
+
+shipments-api is a FastAPI service on PostgreSQL 16 with SQLAlchemy and
+Alembic. Pushes to main deploy it to Fly.io with `flyctl deploy`; a person
+applies migrations afterwards with `fly ssh console -C "alembic upgrade head"`.
+Production's `DATABASE_URL` is a Fly.io secret. CI runs the tests against a
+postgres:16 service container; `tests/conftest.py` creates the tables with
+`Base.metadata.create_all`. The history includes a migration that dropped
+`customers.fax`.
+
+## Decision
+
+Apply migrations in Fly.io's release step, which runs once per deploy on a
+temporary machine before any new machine takes traffic. Migrations that drop
+data are never applied by an automatic step.
+
+- `fly.toml` gains `[deploy] release_command = "python -m app.release"`.
+  `app/release.py` lists the pending revisions with Alembic's script API. If
+  any pending revision drops a table, column, or index (`op.drop_table`,
+  `op.drop_column`, `op.drop_index`), it exits non-zero without migrating;
+  otherwise it runs `alembic upgrade head`.
+- A migration that drops data ships in its own release. A person first takes a
+  backup and verifies that it restores (`pg_dump` to a file, restored into a
+  scratch database), then runs `fly ssh console -C "alembic upgrade head"`,
+  then deploys. `docs/operations.md` describes these steps.
+- The app never migrates at startup and never calls `create_all`.
+
+## Acceptance Coverage
+
+- `AC-001`: the release command applies pending migrations before the new
+  version takes traffic.
+- `AC-002`: a non-zero exit of the release command stops the deploy; the
+  running machines keep serving the previous version.
+- `AC-003`: CI migrates its test database with Alembic before the tests.
+
+## Components
+
+- `fly.toml` (release command), `app/release.py` (new), `tests/conftest.py`,
+  `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `docs/operations.md`. No new service or store.
+
+## Interfaces and Contracts
+
+- Databases are named per environment: `shipments_api_dev` locally,
+  `shipments_api_test` in CI, `shipments_api_prod` in production. The CI
+  service container is renamed from `test` to `shipments_api_test`.
+- Production credentials stay in the Fly.io secret `DATABASE_URL`.
+
+## Data and Control Flow
+
+1. Push to main; the deploy workflow runs `flyctl deploy`.
+2. Fly.io builds the image and runs the release command on a temporary machine.
+3. Exit 0: new machines start and take traffic. Non-zero: the deploy stops and
+   the old machines keep serving.
+
+## Technical Acceptance Criteria
+
+- `AC-001`: after a deploy, `alembic current` in production equals head.
+- `AC-002`: a failing migration leaves the previous release serving.
+- `AC-003`: `tests/conftest.py` runs `alembic upgrade head` against
+  `TEST_DATABASE_URL` once at the start of the test session, replacing
+  `create_all`; CI points it at the PostgreSQL service `shipments_api_test`.
+  Tests never run on SQLite.
+
+## Build Plan
+
+1. Add `app/release.py` and the release command.
+2. Switch `tests/conftest.py` to Alembic; rename the CI database.
+3. Update `docs/operations.md`.
+
+## Risks and Follow-up
+
+- A long migration holds the deploy; keep migrations short.
